    {
      id: "about",
      label: "About",
      icon: "info",
      type: "content",
      markdown: [
        {
          title: "Overview",
          content: [
            "> [!WARNING]",
            "> Confoederatio Dataview is currently a **work-in-progress**.",
            "> This means that you may see placeholder text, misalignment issues, and features that may not display as intended.",
            "",
            "We advise you to not share this URL currently if you have access to it, or to advertise it publicly. Not that we would break your kneecaps, but the website might not always be online in such cases."
          ],
        },
        {
          title: "Data Caveats",
          open: false,
          content: [
            "> [!NOTE]",
            "> Complex multi-raster calculations are downsampled to `1080x540` for performance reasons.",
            "",
            "There are some known issues with NWM2 data we are currently working on.",
            "- Detailed borders are overly reliant on presence modelling/scraping, and as a result of the latter, we cannot make them more available than they currently are until they have been substantially improved.",
            "- Modern borders are often used for statistical purposes in the secondary sources we rely on, and thus bias training data.",
            "- Net migration may not always be predicted accurately for years further back.",
            "",
            "In addition, full data methodologies or releases for Eoscala/Velkscala are a work-in-progress. We try our best to document their methodologies whereever possible.",
            "",
            "If you encounter any issues not documented here, please contact us at [Confoederatio Element](https://element.confoederatio.org)."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Downloads",
          open: false,
          content: [
            "- Atlas 0.51: [Datavault](https://datavault.confoederatio.org/s/rPntqXwCxzXg4Bk)",
            "  - We do not feel that Atlas 0.6 is in a strong position for release; we are working on this.",
            "- Eoscala 1.5: [Datavault](https://datavault.confoederatio.org/s/2Kytdej7ABpw4rr)",
            "- Velkscala 1.0: [Datavault](https://datavault.confoederatio.org/s/44Pfgt7ya8wE77b)",
            "- Stadestér is available as **part of Velkscala**. Whilst separate images are available below, they may be significantly out-of-date.",
            "  - Stadestér 1.1: [Datavault](https://datavault.confoederatio.org/s/KqC3kAKgeKNfWYc)",
            "  - Stadestér 1.0: [Datavault](https://datavault.confoederatio.org/s/CBT74PsEc6tCZFx) | [Zenodo](https://zenodo.org/records/17180328)",
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Era Classification",
          open: false,
          content: [
            "Traditionally, Confoederatio classifies historical time periods into 5 distinct periods for data coverage and statistical purposes. These eras can be viewed in `Date Picker > Bookmarks`, and typically represent common bookends that that were associated with global/macroregional climatic transitions.",
            "1. Era: (10000BC-476AD): Holocene | End of Last Glacial Maximum",
            "2. Era (476AD-1356AD): Traditional end of W. Rome, Gupta contraction | Roman Warm Period-LALIA Transition (Midpoint)",
            "3. Era (1356AD-1815AD): Golden Bull of 1356, Black Death, Red Turbans, Renaissance | End of Mediaeval Warm Period",
            "4. Era (1815AD-1991AD): Concert of Europe, New Imperialism | Industrial Revolution",
            "5. Era (1991AD-): End of the Cold War, Globalisation | End of Widespread Nuclear Testing",
            "In later periods (4. Era and after), climatic transitions tend to be caused by human activity, rather than climate influencing human behaviour. Still, influence cannot be taken as determinism: only with the weight of surrounding human events did they make sense as historical periodisations.",
            "",
            "AD/BC is used for fixed width purposes."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Source Code",
          open: false,
          content: [
            "Source code is available as part of the **Naissance World Model**, specifically in the `histmap/` folder. You can find up-to-date images on either [Github](https://github.com/ConfoederatioVF/Collation/) or [Projects](https://projects.confoederatio.org/c/Collation).",
            "",
            "> [!WARNING]",
            "> We do not recommend using the [Gitlab](https://gitlab.com/confoederatio/research-division/collation) image as it is usually several months out-of-date, and requires registration to view.",
            "",
            "In addition, you should be aware that you will have to download your own versions of input datasets to run the available source code, since they often involve terabytes of data transfer, which is impractical for us to do over Git forges. We are working on ways of making the full image available to others.",
            "",
            "Processing for the NWM is done on a consumer workstation with the following specs:",
            "- CPU: Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900F",
            "- GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER",
            "- RAM: 128GB DDR5 / 256GB Pagefile",
            "- Storage: ~2TB minimum",
            "Given these specs, it takes about 2-3 days for full reproduction."
          ]
        }
      ],
